HolSmtLib is a library for integrating Satisfiability Modulo Theories (SMT)
solvers with the HOL theorem prover.

Files:

COPYRIGHT               Copyright notice, license and disclaimer.
CVC.sml                 Functions to invoke the cvc5 SMT solver.
Holmakefile             Makefile for Holmake (to build selftest.exe).
HolSmtLib.{sig,sml}     Entry point into HolSmtLib. Provides GENERIC_SMT_TAC
                        and derived tactics to call SMT solvers.
HolSmtScript.sml        Various theorems for HolSmtLib.
Library.sml             Common auxiliary functions, tracing.
README                  This file.
TRUSTED_CODE_BASE.md    Checked Z3_TAC boundary, no-oracle gate, and semantic
                        mismatch audit.
selftest.sml            HolSmtLib tests.
SmtLib_Logics.sml       SMT-LIB 2 logics.
SmtLib_Parser.sml       Parsing of SMT-LIB 2 benchmarks.
SmtLib_Theories.sml     SMT-LIB 2 theories.
SmtLib.sml              Translation of HOL terms into SMT-LIB 2 format.
SolverSpec.sml          Definition of SMT solvers.
Unittest.{sig,sml}      Unit tests for HolSmtLib.
Yices.sml               Functions to invoke the Yices SMT solver.
Z3.sml                  Functions to invoke the Z3 SMT solver.
Z3_ProformaThms.sml     Proforma theorems, used for Z3 proof reconstruction.
Z3_Proof.sml            Proof reconstruction for Z3: SML type of Z3 proofs.
Z3_ProofParser.sml      Proof reconstruction for Z3: parsing of Z3's proofs.
Z3_ProofReplay.sml      Proof reconstruction for Z3: replaying Z3's proofs in
                        HOL.

SMT-LIB support matrix:

  Area                         Parse  Typecheck  HOL translate  Replay
  Core Bool/UF                 yes    yes        native         Z3/cvc5 paths
  Int/Real arithmetic          yes    yes        native         partial
  Fixed bit-vectors            yes    yes        native         partial
  ArraysEx select/store        yes    yes        no             no
  Unicode strings              yes    yes        selected native no
  Regular expressions          yes    yes        no             no
  FloatingPoint                yes    yes        no             no
  Datatypes                    yes    single declarations only no no
  Recursive datatypes          AST only explicit rejection no    no
  Z3 Seq/Set/Bag extensions    yes    yes        no             no

HOL translation records include HOLTheoryEncoding rows for the advanced
theories.  These rows distinguish native SMT-LIB encodings from conservative
parser/typechecker embeddings and record proof obligations for the soundness
audit.  Replay is not claimed merely because parsing, typechecking or HOL
translation succeeds.

Trusted-code-base boundary and soundness audit:

`TRUSTED_CODE_BASE.md` documents the checked `Z3_TAC` path, the code that is
inside the audit boundary, and the code that remains outside it, including
`Z3_ORACLE_TAC`.  The generated `.agent-files/SMTLIB_COVERAGE.md` report
contains the cross-referenced "Soundness Audit and Semantic Mismatches" matrix.
Every intentional mismatch must have a checked replay path, a preprocessing
theorem or an explicit unsupported diagnostic.

The current native HOL string translation covers the string sort, STRCAT,
isPREFIX, string_lt and string_le.  It emits SMT-LIB UnicodeStrings symbols;
the semantic mismatch with HOL's char-list strings is deliberately recorded as
a TASK_021 proof obligation.

Higher-order/function-valued HOL terms that would require abstracting function
sorts are rejected deterministically by SmtLib.translate_type/translate_term.
First-order applications such as (P:'a -> bool) x remain supported as
uninterpreted functions.

Z3 version diagnostics and CI hooks:

Z3.sml reports the configured executable and discovered Z3 version through
configured_executable, configured_version and Z3version.  Z3_SMT_Prover adds
that version data path, together with the proof command stem, to proof parse
and replay failures before raising them to HolSmtLib.

Replay diagnostics from Z3_ProofReplay.sml include the proof rule, local proof
subterm, parsed HOL conclusion and a replay-state summary of asserted
hypotheses, definition hypotheses and Z3-created variables.  Unknown proof
rules are reported by Z3_ProofParser.sml with the missing rule name and local
proof subterm.

Z3 th-lemma replay coverage:

  Theory      Collected subkind shapes       Replay status
  arith       farkas, assign-bounds,         checked by existing arith_prove path
              eq-propagate, gomory-cut,
              triangle-eq
  array       select-store, extensionality   checked by existing update prover path
  bv          bit-blast                      checked by existing word/BBLAST path
  basic       eq-propagate                   unsupported diagnostic:
              "unsupported th-lemma shape: theory=basic; checked replay is not
              implemented for basic Boolean/equality simplification lemmas"

Indexed th-lemma failures include theory, subkind, remaining proof indices and
the parsed HOL conclusion in the replay error.

SMT-LIB conformance runner:

The local conformance suite is generated by:

  python3 src/HolSmt/tools/run_conformance_suite.py \
    --out /tmp/holsmt-conformance

The default suite requires no network access.  It generates parser/oracle/proof
smoke inputs for every logic represented by SmtLib_Logics.sml, plus small
metamorphic inputs for operand commutation, variable renaming, nested lets,
scoped assertions and a mixed array/integer case.  The runner writes
`conformance.json`, `CONFORMANCE.md`, proof-corpus JSON, raw Z3 stdout/stderr,
raw proofs and minimized failure repros under the output directory.

Large external benchmark runs are opt-in:

  python3 src/HolSmt/tools/run_conformance_suite.py \
    --out /tmp/holsmt-conformance \
    --benchmark-dir /path/to/smtlib-benchmarks \
    --z3-proof-dir /path/to/z3/proof/tests

Use `--logic` and repeated `--mode` flags to restrict a run.  The typecheck-only
and end-to-end Z3_TAC modes are command-template hooks so CI can plug in a HOL
driver without making the default Python suite depend on a particular heap:

  python3 src/HolSmt/tools/run_conformance_suite.py \
    --mode typecheck-only \
    --typecheck-command 'my-holsmt-typecheck {input} {logic}' \
    --mode z3-tac \
    --z3-tac-command 'my-z3-tac-check {input} {logic}'

Unconfigured hooks are counted as `unsupported`, not hidden.  Unsupported
counts are grouped by logic, mode, SMT-LIB target version and discovered Z3
version in the generated reports.

Pull-request CI runs the PolyML expk build against the Z3 versions already
provided by the docker-ci base image: 2.19.1, 4.12.4 and 4.13.0.  The
equivalent local hook is:

  docker buildx build \
    --build-arg SML=poly \
    --build-arg Z3_VERSION=<2.19.1|4.12.4|4.13.0> \
    --build-arg CVC_VERSION=5 \
    --build-arg CSDP_VERSION=1 \
    --build-arg 'BUILDOPTS=--no-cache --expk -j4 -t' \
    -f developers/docker-ci/Dockerfile .

The HolSmt selftest is part of that build.  `Z3_SMT_Prover` and selftest
theorem checks reject unexpected oracle/axiom tags on `Z3_TAC` outputs; `sat`
and `unknown` solver results are negative outcomes and must not produce HOL
theorems.

Further documentation can be found in the HOL Description (in
HOL/Manual/Description).
